//
// LEGAL POSITIONING NOTE — READ BEFORE EDITING. STRICTEST TIER:
// Albania sits with GREECE, CROATIA and the NETHERLANDS.
// - Law No. 69/2012 on the pre-university education system, as
//   amended (56/2015, 48/2018, 44/2023 among others), provides that
//   FULL-TIME BASIC EDUCATION IS COMPULSORY for all children
//   resident in the Republic of Albania FROM THE AGE OF SIX TO THE
//   AGE OF SIXTEEN, save for cases provided in the law itself. The
//   obligation is therefore framed by both the basic-education
//   programme and the age of sixteen — state it that way.
// - Parental-choice homeschooling is NOT established in Albanian
//   law. Say so plainly and first.
// - THE ONE HOME PROVISION IS STATE-ADMINISTERED AND HEALTH-BASED:
//   the LOCAL EDUCATION UNIT provides "arsimim në shtëpi" —
//   education at home — to students who cannot attend an ordinary
//   or specialised basic-education school, according to criteria
//   and procedures set by JOINT INSTRUCTION of the Minister of
//   Education and the Minister of Health. It is a welfare measure
//   delivered by the state, not a parental route. State it
//   factually; never position it, never advise toward it.
// - LANGUAGE: the language of education in Albanian institutions is
//   Albanian, with provisions for national minorities.
// - CERTIFICATES: basic education ends with the dëftesa e arsimit
//   bazë after the national basic-education examinations; upper
//   secondary ends with the Matura Shtetërore diploma after the
//   national matura examinations.
// - THE WINDOW: upper secondary (gjimnaz or vocational) is NOT
//   compulsory, and the compulsory obligation ends at sixteen. So
//   the A-Level years after sixteen sit outside the obligation
//   entirely. Use prominently — but note the boundary is AGE
//   SIXTEEN, not simply the end of grade 9, because the statute
//   frames it by age. Do not claim a window opens at fourteen or
//   fifteen.
// SO: SUPPLEMENTARY IS THE DEFAULT during the compulsory years —
// the school enrolment carries the obligation, Cambridge runs
// alongside in the after-school slot. Full-time Smartious is for
// the post-16 phase and for non-resident families under another
// country's framework.
// RESIDENCY: the obligation attaches to children resident in
// Albania. Non-resident families follow their country of residence.
// State precisely; refer to families' own advisers. Relevant given
// the tourism, second-home, and remote-work inflow since 2021.
// MARKET NOTE: the international tier is a Tirana story — Tirana
// International School, the Albanian College Tirana, the World
// Academy of Tirana, Memorial and the Turkish-founded schools, plus
// the Italian and French provision. Durrës has a little; Vlorë,
// Shkodër, Elbasan, Fier and the Riviera have essentially none.
// Economy: a tourism boom that has reshaped the coast since 2021,
// the Durrës port and logistics, the Patos-Marinza oilfield and
// Fier's energy belt, hydropower on the Drin, a growing BPO and
// call-centre sector in Tirana serving Italian and German markets,
// and one of Europe's largest diasporas relative to population
